WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
How do you measure opposite pressures inside a living stem?

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.160
Evaporation pulls water up dead xylem pipes under tension, below zero.

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.960
Living phloem tubes push sugar sap under positive pressure.

4
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.650
Start with xylem tension.

5
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.210
Seal a cut leaf in a steel Scholander pressure chamber.

6
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.450
Raise gas pressure until sap just appears at the cut.

7
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.970
That pressure balances the xylem's tension.

8
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:37.510
So the shoot's water potential, water's energy relative to pure water, is roughly

9
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.570
minus that pressure.

10
00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:44.063
Now phloem: its sieve tubes, chains of living cells, carry sugar.

11
00:00:45.323 --> 00:00:49.763
An aphid pushes its thin mouthpart, a stylet, into one sieve tube.

12
00:00:51.043 --> 00:00:54.203
Cut the aphid away, leaving only the open stylet.

13
00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:58.463
Does sap pull back inside, stop, or keep oozing out?

14
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:08.383
Sap keeps oozing, pushed out by positive pressure inside the sieve tube.

15
00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:11.723
The ooze is nearly pure phloem sap.

16
00:01:12.843 --> 00:01:18.003
To measure that pressure, called turgor, a glass pico-gauge enters one living sieve

17
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:22.103
tube. Its tip holds a tiny trapped volume of oil.

18
00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:27.723
How far sap squeezes the oil reads the pressure inside one working cell.

19
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:31.347
Pressure alone does not give flow speed.

20
00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:38.207
Feed a leaf carbon dioxide labelled with radioactive carbon-11; it makes labelled

21
00:01:38.207 --> 00:01:42.127
sugar. Detectors along the stem time its arrival.

22
00:01:43.547 --> 00:01:47.467
Distance between detectors divided by travel time gives speed.

23
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:54.490
Physiologists count embolisms, gas bubbles that break xylem water columns, to judge

24
00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:00.210
drought damage. But cutting a tense stem under water can itself create embolisms.

25
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:07.650
X-ray microtomography merges angled X-ray images into three-dimensional stem scans.

26
00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:13.450
Air-filled and water-filled pipes look different, so scanning before and after

27
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.270
cutting exposes false bubbles.

28
00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.730
Rehydrating first relaxes tension to test the cause.

29
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.830
Phloem measurements have limits too.

30
00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:29.010
In one key study, pressure at the root end came from root cortex cells, not sieve

31
00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.710
tubes. So the real pressure drop along the tubes may be smaller.

32
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:39.230
Its numbers hold for one species; oak data were removed during review.

33
00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.280
These tools unlocked two results.

34
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:49.200
In 2015, Torres-Ruiz and colleagues found that cutting under water while xylem was

35
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.940
under tension itself created embolisms.

36
00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.860
It occurred in four species, varying with species and tension.

37
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.260
So counts from cut stems can overstate drought damage.

38
00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:08.823
In 2016, Knoblauch, Holbrook and colleagues tested Münch's 1930 idea in morning

39
00:03:08.823 --> 00:03:14.963
glory. Münch proposed that sugar loaded at a source leaf raises pressure, pushing

40
00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:16.883
sap toward where sugar is used.

41
00:03:18.403 --> 00:03:22.563
Critics argued long, narrow sieve tubes would need more pressure than living cells

42
00:03:22.563 --> 00:03:25.763
could hold. So the team lengthened vines.

43
00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:32.997
Source turgor rose from about 0.75 to more than 2.2 MPa.

44
00:03:32.997 --> 00:03:37.297
Sieve tubes also conducted five to six times better.

45
00:03:38.537 --> 00:03:42.237
Together, pressure flow's estimated reach matched the vine's length.
